+ *                a PAGE_READWRITE heap block counts as executable, so
+ *                InvalidateIntervalInternal takes the mutex.
+ *   thread 0284  holds CodeInvalidationMutex -- taken here, at this function's
+ *                first statement -- and the loader section, and waits for the
+ *                heap section.
+ *
+ * The second edge is this one. The mutex was acquired as the first statement
+ * and held across LoadImageRelocations, the MappedImages insert,
+ * GetBaseFilename, fmt::format, std::filesystem::exists/create_directories,
+ * CodeMapWriter construction and file I/O, and LoadAOTImages -- and several of
+ * those allocate from the *Win32 process heap*, not from rpmalloc.
+ * std::filesystem and the CodeMapWriter's file open go through kernelbase, and
+ * LoadAOTImages builds a ScopedUnicodeString, whose
